ADS1115
=======

ADS1115 supports much higher SPS (Samples Per Second) than 170. Worked around partially by extending ct_clamp sample_duration to 1000ms
[21:08:36][D][ct_clamp:038]: 'Fridge AC Current' - Raw AC Value: 0.005A after 34 different samples (170 SPS)


ct_clamp does not seem to use more than 3 decimals of accuracy during calculations, which is a limitation with higher current CTs
[01:32:26][D][ct_clamp:038]: 'Fridge AC Current' - Raw AC Value: 0.004A after 167 different samples (167 SPS)

At low consumption levels, some current measurements turn negative after the calibrate_polynomial. How to set to zero in lambda?
[21:21:38][D][sensor:113]: 'Fridge AC Power': Sending state -0.00749 W with 1 decimals of accuracy


NOTE : measured Amps times measured Volts = apparent power > active power


Learning something from another sensor, to make voltage readings better than using ct_clamp
===========================================================================================
And hopefully integrate correct and reliable line voltage measurement using the same ESP32 as the one for power measurements :
https://community.home-assistant.io/t/zmpt101b-precision-voltage-sensor-module/124617/7
"""
- Increase the I2C bus to something much faster than the default 50 kHz, may be necessary to get more samples taken from ADS1115 ADCs
"""

Done on FEB08@20.30 approximately, one can easily see measurements to be more stable (less variance) and the number of SPS to be higher than with the default I2C frequency.

As this continued over time, we did increase frequency to 800kHz, with per-circuit re-calibration pending for the future.



